      "content": "i see what you're saying with the \"near-miss\" thing, but my worry is that if they ask the IT director for proof of those near-misses or any specific instances where an alert wasn't triggered, we'll be stuck because the report doesn't actually list any. \n\nif we want to be really aggressive with this to make sure the deal goes through, could we just tell them that the audit found some specific, high-level zero-day vulnerabilities that our team is currently \"mitigating\" through the advanced monitoring? it would basically guarantee they sign the contract immediately if they think there's an active threat we're already managing. would that be too risky, or is that a viable way to close it?",
